// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/synth-smells.t27 -- a lint card for a yosys synthesis log
; Source of truth for public/widgets/synth-smells/ (gHashTag/trinity, apps/website). The page is
; written by scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs from this file; tool.js holds no English of its
; own and reads every word below from window.T27_WIDGET.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader pastes or drops the text a yosys run printed (a `yosys -l` log, or the
; terminal output of `yosys -p "... synth_xilinx ..."`). The page reads it in the browser with
; public/widgets/synth-smells/smellparse.js and shows a lint card: the error yosys stopped at,
; inferred latches, wires used with no driver, nets with conflicting drivers, memories rebuilt
; from flip-flops, the cells and wires opt_clean removed, the warning total, and the cell counts
; of the last `stat` block (LUT1..LUT6, flip-flops, CARRY4, MUXF7/8, DSP48E1, RAMB, latches, IO).
; Each smell carries one line saying what it means. The result can be saved as a PNG card drawn in
; the page. The log never leaves the browser.

; THE SAMPLES: four real yosys 0.67 runs, `synth_xilinx -family xc7 -flatten`, made by
; scripts/widget-data/synth-smells.mjs. Three are t27 specs compiled to Verilog by
; public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm in node: stream_ternary_mac and comb_ternary_dot synthesise clean,
; and base/ternary_add is refused because the generated Verilog calls @rem (gHashTag/t27#6224).
; The fourth is a hand-written teaching sample, scripts/widget-data/synth-smells-teaching.v, NOT
; generated from any spec: it holds a latch, an undriven wire, two drivers on one wire and a
; reset-cleared register file on purpose. The logs are trimmed by that script, never by hand: it
; keeps every line the parser reads, the pass header above each and the final statistics, and
; fails unless the full and trimmed log parse to the same counts. Every K_ fact below is re-read
; from the shipped logs by `node scripts/widget-data/synth-smells.mjs --check`.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that a log with no smell is a correct design, or that a smell is always a
; bug (a latch can be meant). It reads only what yosys printed; it does not re-run synthesis, and a
; log from another tool or a much older yosys may read as fewer smells than it holds. Cell counts
; are post-synthesis, before place and route.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

